IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-offences`

-- offences: tests of ccc11-offences.l4 (Part VIII.1, sections 320.13 to 320.18: the offences and their exceptions)
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the provision, beside each assertion, before the run; none is copied from the code's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: the text says yes / the text says no in its own words / not covered.


§ `s 320.13(1): operates a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public`
-- arguments: operated (by s 320.11) ; dangerous manner
#ASSERT `s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- operated and dangerous
#ASSERT `s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the manner was not dangerous
#ASSERT `s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate (s 320.11 "operate means")
#ASSERT `s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the person operated is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not dangerous: a no whatever the operate answer

§ `s 320.13(2): dangerous operation and, as a result, bodily harm to another person`
-- arguments: operated ; dangerous ; as a result caused harm to another person ; the harm is bodily harm (by s 2)
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all elements
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the harm was not "bodily harm" (s 2: more than transient or trifling)
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the harm is bodily harm is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no harm resulted from the operation
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not dangerous
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate
#ASSERT `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- harm is not bodily harm: a no beats a not-covered

§ `s 320.13(3): dangerous operation and, as a result, the death of another person`
#ASSERT `s 320.13(3) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes the death of another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all elements
#ASSERT `s 320.13(3) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes the death of another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no death resulted
#ASSERT `s 320.13(3) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes the death of another person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not dangerous
#ASSERT `s 320.13(3) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes the death of another person` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the person operated is not covered

§ `s 320.14(1)(a): operates a conveyance while the ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(a) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while their ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- operated while impaired
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(a) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while their ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not impaired to any degree
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(a) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while their ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(a) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while their ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.14(1)(b): a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more in 100 mL within two hours after ceasing to operate`
-- arguments: operated ; blood alcohol concentration ; the exception of subsection (5) applies (by s 320.14(5))
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 80 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- exactly 80: "equal to or exceeds 80"
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 79 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 79 is below 80
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 79.9 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 79.9 is below 80
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 200 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- well above 80
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 80 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if": the exception applies
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 80 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the exception applies is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST FALSE) 100 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate (so did not "cease to operate")
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (JUST TRUE) 50 NOTHING EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- below 80: a no whatever the exception answer

§ `s 320.14(1)(c): a blood drug concentration at or above the concentration prescribed by regulation (an input)`
-- arguments: operated ; the person's concentration ; the prescribed concentration ; the exception of subsection (6) applies
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` (JUST TRUE) 2 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- at the prescribed concentration: "equal to or exceeds"
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` (JUST TRUE) 1.9 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- below the prescribed concentration
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` (JUST TRUE) 7 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- above it
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` (JUST TRUE) 2 2 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the exception of subsection (6) applies
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` (JUST FALSE) 7 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` NOTHING 7 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.14(1)(d): alcohol and drug concentrations both at or above those prescribed for the combination (inputs)`
-- arguments: operated ; blood alcohol concentration ; blood drug concentration ; prescribed alcohol ; prescribed drug ; the exception of subsection (7) applies
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` (JUST TRUE) 50 1 50 1 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- both exactly at the prescribed concentrations
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` (JUST TRUE) 49 1 50 1 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- alcohol below the prescribed concentration
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` (JUST TRUE) 50 0.9 50 1 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- drug below the prescribed concentration
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` (JUST TRUE) 90 5 50 1 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the exception of subsection (7) applies
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` NOTHING 90 5 50 1 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.14(1): the offence is committed under any of paragraphs (a) to (d)`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- paragraph (a) alone
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- paragraph (b) alone
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- paragraph (c) alone
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- paragraph (d) alone
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- none of (a) to (d)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) not covered and the others say no
#ASSERT `s 320.14(1) everyone commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (b) holds whatever (a) says

§ `s 320.14(2): an offence under subsection (1) and, while operating the conveyance, bodily harm to another person`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and bodily harm caused
#ASSERT `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no harm caused while operating
#ASSERT `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the harm was not bodily harm
#ASSERT `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- bodily harm not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence under (1) is not covered

§ `s 320.14(3): an offence under subsection (1) and, while operating the conveyance, the death of another person`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes the death of another person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and a death caused
#ASSERT `s 320.14(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes the death of another person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no death caused
#ASSERT `s 320.14(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes the death of another person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes the death of another person` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence under (1) is not covered

§ `s 320.14(4): a blood drug concentration at or above the concentration prescribed for (4) and less than that prescribed for paragraph (1)(c) (inputs)`
-- arguments: operated ; the person's concentration ; prescribed for (4) ; prescribed for (1)(c) ; the exception of subsection (6) applies
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` (JUST TRUE) 2 2 5 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- exactly the lower prescribed concentration
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` (JUST TRUE) 4.9 2 5 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- just under the (1)(c) concentration
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` (JUST TRUE) 5 2 5 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- at the (1)(c) concentration: not "less than" it (that is paragraph (1)(c)'s)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` (JUST TRUE) 1.9 2 5 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- below the lower concentration
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` (JUST TRUE) 3 2 5 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the exception of subsection (6) applies ("or subsection (4)")
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` (JUST FALSE) 3 2 5 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate
#ASSERT `s 320.14(4) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a low blood drug concentration` NOTHING 3 2 5 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.14(5): alcohol exception: consumed after ceasing to operate; no reasonable expectation of a demand; consumption consistent with the concentration and with under 80 at the time (two limbs)`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all of (a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (a) unmet: this subsection gives no exception on these facts
#ASSERT `s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (b) unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (c) first limb unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (c) second limb unmet

§ `s 320.14(6): drug exception: consumed the drug after ceasing to operate; no reasonable expectation of being required to provide a sample of a bodily substance`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(6) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or subsection 320.14(4)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (a) and (b)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(6) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or subsection 320.14(4)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (a) unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.14(6) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or subsection 320.14(4)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (b) unmet

§ `s 320.14(7): combination exception: consumed the drug or the alcohol or both; no reasonable expectation; consumption consistent (two limbs)`
#ASSERT `s 320.14(7) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(d)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all of (a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `s 320.14(7) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(d)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (a) unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.14(7) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(d)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (b) unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.14(7) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(d)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (c) first limb unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.14(7) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(d)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (c) second limb unmet

§ `s 320.15(1): knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply, without reasonable excuse, with a demand made under 320.27 or 320.28`
-- arguments: knew a demand had been made ; failed or refused to comply ; had a reasonable excuse ; the demand was made under 320.27 or 320.28 (by those sections)
#ASSERT `s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all elements
#ASSERT `s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not know that a demand had been made
#ASSERT `s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- complied
#ASSERT `s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the demand was not one made under 320.27 or 320.28
#ASSERT `s 320.15(1) everyone commits an offence who, knowing that a demand has been made, fails or refuses to comply with it without reasonable excuse` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the demand was one made under those sections is not covered

§ `s 320.15(2) and (3): the offence under (1) and knowledge of, or recklessness as to, an accident resulting in bodily harm, or death`
#ASSERT `s 320.15(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and the mens rea of (2)
#ASSERT `s 320.15(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no knowledge or recklessness as to bodily harm
#ASSERT `s 320.15(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.15(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence under (1) is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.15(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in death` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and the mens rea of (3)
#ASSERT `s 320.15(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in death` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no knowledge or recklessness as to a death
#ASSERT `s 320.15(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.15(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, they were involved in an accident that resulted in death` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)

§ `s 320.15(4): a person convicted under this section is not to be convicted of another offence under this section for the same transaction`
#ASSERT `s 320.15(4) the person is barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 with respect to the same transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- barred: convicted, another offence under the section, same transaction
#ASSERT `s 320.15(4) the person is barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 with respect to the same transaction` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not convicted of an offence under this section
#ASSERT `s 320.15(4) the person is barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 with respect to the same transaction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the other offence is not under this section
#ASSERT `s 320.15(4) the person is barred from being convicted of another offence under section 320.15 with respect to the same transaction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- a different transaction

§ `s 320.16(1): operates, knows or is reckless as to an accident, and without reasonable excuse fails to stop, give name and address, and (if a person is injured or appears to need help) offer assistance`
-- arguments: operated ; knew or reckless as to the accident ; failed to stop ; failed to give name and address ; a person injured or appeared to need assistance ; failed to offer assistance ; reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- failed to stop
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- stopped but did not give name and address
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- stopped and gave name, but did not offer assistance to an injured person
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no one injured or needing assistance: no duty to offer it, so no failure
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- injured person, and assistance was offered
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not know and was not reckless as to the accident
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate
#ASSERT `s 320.16(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance, knows that or is reckless as to whether it has been involved in an accident, and fails without reasonable excuse to stop, give their name and address and offer assistance` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.16(2) and (3): the offence under (1) and knowledge of, or recklessness as to, bodily harm, or death`
#ASSERT `s 320.16(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and the mens rea of (2)
#ASSERT `s 320.16(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no knowledge or recklessness
#ASSERT `s 320.16(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in bodily harm` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no offence under (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.16(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in death` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an offence under (1) and the mens rea of (3)
#ASSERT `s 320.16(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in death` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no knowledge or recklessness
#ASSERT `s 320.16(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.16(1) and knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the accident resulted in death` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence under (1) is not covered

§ `s 320.17: operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop as soon as is reasonable`
-- arguments: operated ; motor vehicle (by s 2) ; vessel (by 320.11) ; being pursued ; the pursuer was a peace officer (by s 2) ; failed to stop as soon as reasonable ; reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a motor vehicle
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a vessel
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- neither a motor vehicle nor a vessel (an aircraft, say)
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not being pursued
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- stopped as soon as reasonable
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- with a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the pursuer was a peace officer is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the pursuer was not a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 320.17 everyone commits an offence who operates a motor vehicle or vessel while being pursued by a peace officer and fails without reasonable excuse to stop` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.18(1): operates a conveyance while prohibited by an order made under the Act or by another legal restriction in respect of a conviction under the Act or a discharge under 730`
-- arguments: operated ; prohibited by an order made under this Act ; prohibited by another legal restriction ; the exception of subsection (2) applies (by s 320.18(2))
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- paragraph (a)
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- prohibited by neither
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the interlock exception of subsection (2) applies
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the exception applies is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- did not operate
#ASSERT `s 320.18(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while prohibited from doing so` NOTHING TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- operation not covered

§ `s 320.18(2): no offence under (1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle if registered in an interlock program and complying with its conditions`
#ASSERT `s 320.18(2) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under subsection 320.18(1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a motor vehicle, registered, complying
#ASSERT `s 320.18(2) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under subsection 320.18(1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not registered
#ASSERT `s 320.18(2) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under subsection 320.18(1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- registered but not complying
#ASSERT `s 320.18(2) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under subsection 320.18(1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not a motor vehicle: this subsection gives no exception
#ASSERT `s 320.18(2) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under subsection 320.18(1) arising out of the operation of a motor vehicle` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it is a motor vehicle is not covered

